      "stageRecord": "The buying VP is expanded into an embedded IP with PRO generated in Spec-IP and a silent nonfinite I. ซื้อ assigns its external Buyer role to PRO, rather than sharing that role directly with the matrix subject. Under the classical GB PRO theorem, the embedded subject position is ungoverned: the nonfinite I does not govern PRO, and C does not govern into Spec-IP. A silent purposive C then projects CP, which is right-adjoined to the matrix V′ containing วิ่ง ไป. The resulting binary adjunction preserves the surface order while locating the purpose boundary after ไป. The purpose relation connects the motion event to the intended buying event; actual completion of the purchase is not asserted by that relation. The analysis thus commits to a covert purposive clause, not an overtly missing word in the input. PRO's controller is established only when the matrix subject enters its clause.",
