      "stageRecord": "The matrix IP is assembled with เขา directly in Spec-IP, a silent clause-level I, and the motion VP containing its purpose adjunct. First, the matrix motion predicate assigns its composite Agent–Mover role to เขา. Second, matrix I licenses abstract nominative Case on that overt subject, without introducing an overt agreement marker or a determinate tense value. Third, the matrix subject obligatorily controls embedded PRO: เขา c-commands the purpose clause and supplies the reference of its independently theta-marked subject. Control is not movement, so เขา has no lower copy or trace inside the buying clause. The overt subject receives only its matrix theta-role, while PRO receives the buying role, preserving the theta criterion. Finally, the five overt terminals are associated with the exact unspaced input เขาวิ่งไปซื้อข้าว; the silent purpose head, embedded I, and PRO contribute no pronounced material. This yields the reading ‘he runs/goes in order to buy rice,’ with a separate controlled purpose clause.",
